1
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:04,880
Lord, cast your light upon us.

2
00:02:05,270 --> 00:02:07,270
Lord of Light, defend us.

3
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:11,880
Show us the truth.

4
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:14,340
Strike this man down if he is guilty.

5
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:16,850
Give strength to his sword if he is true.

6
00:02:17,790 --> 00:02:20,940
Lord of Light, give us wisdom.

7
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,930
For the night is dark

8
00:02:28,790 --> 00:02:30,060
and full of terrors.

9
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:32,690
For the night is dark and full of terrors.

10
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:56,070
Get back.

11
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:27,710
Guilty. Guilty. Guilty.

12
00:04:27,890 --> 00:04:30,320
Guilty. Guilty. Guilty.

13
00:04:30,510 --> 00:04:33,240
Guilty. Guilty. Guilty.

14
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:34,950
Guilty. Guilty. Guilty.

15
00:04:34,950 --> 00:04:36,120
Kill him!

16
00:04:55,170 --> 00:04:57,200
Lord, cast your light upon this man, your servant.

17
00:04:57,290 --> 00:04:58,820
Bring him back from death and darkness.

18
00:04:58,820 --> 00:05:00,040
His flame has been extinguished.

19
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:00,900
Restore it.

20
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:03,920
For the night is dark and full of terrors.

21
00:05:03,930 --> 00:05:05,930
- Lord, cast... - Arya, don't!

22
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:08,280
Bring him back from death and darkness...

23
00:05:08,550 --> 00:05:09,430
No!

24
00:05:09,510 --> 00:05:12,650
Let go of me! Let me go!

25
00:05:12,650 --> 00:05:16,180
Looks like their God likes me more than your butcher's boy.

26
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:17,730
Burn in hell!

27
00:05:18,470 --> 00:05:19,410
He will.

28
00:05:23,790 --> 00:05:24,940
But not today.

29
00:05:50,170 --> 00:05:53,030
Orell says there are crows patrolling on the Wall.

30
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:54,570
Tell me what you know.

31
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,010
There are four to a patrol--

32
00:05:57,710 --> 00:05:59,260
two builders to check for structural damage,

33
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:00,760
two rangers to watch for enemies.

34
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,830
How often do these patrols go out?

35
00:06:04,180 --> 00:06:05,380
It varies.

36
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:08,540
If I knew where on the Wall we were heading, I could tell you.

37
00:06:08,750 --> 00:06:09,960
You'd like to know that.

38
00:06:13,290 --> 00:06:15,780
There are 19 castles guarding the Wall.

39
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:18,820
How many are manned?

40
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:21,340
Three.

41
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:23,040
You sure of that?

42
00:06:26,530 --> 00:06:27,280
Which three?

43
00:06:30,910 --> 00:06:31,890
Castle Black.

44
00:06:32,870 --> 00:06:34,040
Aye, Castle Black.

45
00:06:34,450 --> 00:06:36,080
Everyone knows Castle Black.

46
00:06:36,340 --> 00:06:37,230
Which others?

47
00:06:43,590 --> 00:06:44,970
Eastwatch-by-the-Sea

48
00:06:46,010 --> 00:06:47,180
and the Shadow Tower.

49
00:06:50,970 --> 00:06:53,030
How many men remain in Castle Black?

50
00:06:53,090 --> 00:06:54,730
- 1,000. - Liar.

51
00:06:56,590 --> 00:06:58,830
What happens to your eagle after I kill you?

52
00:06:58,970 --> 00:07:01,630
Does he drift away like a kite with his strings cut

53
00:07:02,170 --> 00:07:03,550
or does he just flop dead to the ground?

54
00:07:03,550 --> 00:07:04,790
He's no crow.

55
00:07:04,790 --> 00:07:07,580
Just 'cause you want him inside you don't make him one of us.

56
00:07:07,580 --> 00:07:09,010
I'm not afraid of you.

57
00:07:16,710 --> 00:07:18,100
I like you, boy.

58
00:07:19,310 --> 00:07:20,590
But if you lie to me,

59
00:07:21,410 --> 00:07:24,310
I'll pull your guts out through your throat.

60
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:28,780
1,000 men.

61
00:07:34,710 --> 00:07:36,740
We'll find out soon enough.

62
00:07:43,990 --> 00:07:45,750
I don't need you to protect me.

63
00:07:46,020 --> 00:07:47,110
Of course you do.

64
00:07:47,450 --> 00:07:49,560
Who stopped Rattleshirt when he was about to cut your throat?

65
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:51,760
Who vouched for you with Mance?

66
00:07:52,740 --> 00:07:54,540
It seems you owe me a debt.

67
00:07:56,340 --> 00:07:58,580
- Give it back. - Well, I stole it.

68
00:07:58,780 --> 00:08:02,310
It's mine. If you want it, come steal it back.

69
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:05,350
Ygritte!

70
00:08:07,390 --> 00:08:08,190
Ygritte!

71
00:08:13,210 --> 00:08:15,890
Ygritte! Seven hells.

72
00:08:16,130 --> 00:08:17,040
Ygritte!

73
00:08:21,430 --> 00:08:22,490
Is Orell right?

74
00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:25,560
Are you still a crow?

75
00:08:27,580 --> 00:08:28,980
It's time you proved yourself.

76
00:08:31,610 --> 00:08:33,370
- Ygritte. - You swore some vows.

77
00:08:35,410 --> 00:08:36,830
I want you to break 'em.

78
00:08:39,850 --> 00:08:41,070
I want you to see me.

79
00:08:44,870 --> 00:08:45,700
All of me.

80
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:01,620
We shouldn't.

81
00:09:04,950 --> 00:09:05,830
We should.

82
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:27,810
Why are you still dressed?

83
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:31,190
You know nothing, Jon Sno--

84
00:09:46,330 --> 00:09:47,520
That thing you did

85
00:09:48,330 --> 00:09:49,510
with your mouth--

86
00:09:52,070 --> 00:09:54,630
is that what lords do to their ladies in the South?

87
00:09:55,450 --> 00:09:56,270
I don't know.

88
00:09:56,860 --> 00:09:58,610
I just wanted to kiss you there is all.

89
00:10:00,590 --> 00:10:01,680
You seemed to like it.

90
00:10:02,590 --> 00:10:03,800
Aye, I liked it some.

91
00:10:04,260 --> 00:10:05,220
Who taught you that?

92
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:08,570
There's been no one else. Only you.

93
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:10,060
A maid.

94
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:12,790
You were a maid.

95
00:10:13,170 --> 00:10:15,130
I was a man of the Night's Watch.

96
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:18,920
How about you? Were you a maid?

97
00:10:19,470 --> 00:10:20,490
What do you think?

98
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:23,100
- Who was he? - Just a boy.

99
00:10:23,950 --> 00:10:25,700
He came trading with his brothers.

100
00:10:26,510 --> 00:10:29,540
He had red hair like me. Kissed by fire.

101
00:10:29,550 --> 00:10:30,330
But...

102
00:10:31,790 --> 00:10:32,760
he was weak.

103
00:10:34,410 --> 00:10:35,240
Not like you.

104
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:37,410
That was the first one.

105
00:10:37,410 --> 00:10:39,660
Then there was this Thenn boy.

106
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,750
Spoke no Common, but gods, he was built like a mammoth.

107
00:10:42,750 --> 00:10:45,620
Yeah, thanks. I think I've heard enough.

108
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:50,410
We'd best get back.

109
00:10:50,820 --> 00:10:51,590
Tormund--

110
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:57,160
I'm not done with you yet.

111
00:11:04,670 --> 00:11:06,600
How long's it been since you had a bath?

112
00:11:23,020 --> 00:11:24,260
Let's not go back.

113
00:11:26,370 --> 00:11:28,210
Let's stay here a while longer.

114
00:11:31,510 --> 00:11:34,060
I don't ever want to leave this cave, Jon Snow.

115
00:11:36,690 --> 00:11:37,530
Not ever.

116
00:11:49,310 --> 00:11:50,300
I want my gold.

117
00:11:50,300 --> 00:11:51,590
It says it clearly right there on that note

118
00:11:51,590 --> 00:11:53,500
you'll be repaid in full when the war is over.

119
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:55,830
Piss on that! You're nothing but thieves.

120
00:11:55,830 --> 00:11:58,470
We're outlaws. Outlaws steal.

121
00:11:58,560 --> 00:11:59,630
You're lucky we didn't kill you.

122
00:11:59,630 --> 00:12:00,690
Come try it, archer.

123
00:12:00,690 --> 00:12:02,580
I'll shove those arrows up your ass.

124
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:04,770
You can't let him go. He's a murderer. He's guilty.

125
00:12:04,770 --> 00:12:06,980
- Not in the eyes of god. - You can't!

126
00:12:06,980 --> 00:12:09,860
Enough! The judgment isn't ours to make.

127
00:12:13,450 --> 00:12:15,260
Go in peace, Sandor Clegane.

128
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:18,200
The Lord of Light isn't done with you yet.

129
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,660
Riders coming through!

130
00:12:36,810 --> 00:12:37,630
The Kingslayer.

131
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:38,760
Down!

132
00:12:39,430 --> 00:12:40,570
On your knees.

133
00:12:41,290 --> 00:12:45,030
Lord Bolton, I give you the Kingslayer.

134
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:47,830
Pick him up, Locke.

135
00:12:54,820 --> 00:12:55,460
You've lost a hand.

136
00:12:55,460 --> 00:12:58,740
No, my lord, he has it here.

137
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:04,480
- Take this away. - Send it to his father?

138
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:06,480
You'll hold your tongue unless you want to lose it.

139
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:10,150
Cut her free. Apologies, my lady.

140
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:12,460
You're under my protection now.

141
00:13:12,550 --> 00:13:14,900
Thank you, my lord.

142
00:13:18,330 --> 00:13:20,350
Find suitable rooms for our guests.

143
00:13:21,420 --> 00:13:22,450
We'll speak later.

144
00:13:25,020 --> 00:13:25,790
Lord Bolton.

145
00:13:30,230 --> 00:13:32,100
Is there word from the capital?

146
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:34,640
You haven't heard?

147
00:13:36,110 --> 00:13:38,770
Stannis Baratheon laid siege to King's Landing.

148
00:13:39,140 --> 00:13:40,720
Sailed into Blackwater Bay.

149
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:44,000
Stormed the gates with thousands of men.

150
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:47,330
And your sister...

151
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:54,440
How can I put this?

152
00:13:57,330 --> 00:13:58,430
Your sister...

153
00:14:00,870 --> 00:14:02,080
is alive and well.

154
00:14:03,020 --> 00:14:05,110
Your father's forces prevailed.

155
00:14:07,460 --> 00:14:08,710
Ser Jaime isn't well.

156
00:14:10,170 --> 00:14:11,260
Take him to Qyburn.

157
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:32,740
- Will I die? - No.

158
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:34,760
The corruption has spread.

159
00:14:34,770 --> 00:14:36,680
I fear it must be cut away.

160
00:14:36,850 --> 00:14:40,140
The safest course would be to take the whole arm off.

161
00:14:40,390 --> 00:14:41,550
Then you'll die.

162
00:14:44,330 --> 00:14:45,650
You're no maester.

163
00:14:46,990 --> 00:14:47,960
Where's your chain?

164
00:14:49,780 --> 00:14:51,380
The Citadel stripped me of it.

165
00:14:51,570 --> 00:14:54,130
They found some of my experiments

166
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:55,790
too bold.

167
00:14:56,700 --> 00:14:59,740
I can leave your upper arm, make the cut at your elbow.

168
00:15:00,280 --> 00:15:02,850
I don't need my right hand to kill you.

169
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:07,050
I can take away the rotting flesh

170
00:15:07,750 --> 00:15:09,960
and try and burn out the corruption

171
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:12,030
with boiling wine.

172
00:15:12,710 --> 00:15:14,320
With any luck, that will suffice.

173
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:17,020
You'll need milk of the poppy.

174
00:15:18,530 --> 00:15:20,790
- No milk of the poppy. - There will be pain.

175
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,860
- I'll scream. - Quite a bit of pain.

176
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:25,800
I'll scream loudly.

177
00:16:01,010 --> 00:16:02,040
Lord Baelish.

178
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:03,730
Your Grace.

179
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:05,880
I wonder if I might ask you for a favor.

180
00:16:06,190 --> 00:16:06,690
Of course, Your Grace.

181
00:16:06,690 --> 00:16:08,430
I have reason to believe that House Tyrell

182
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:10,730
do not hold the crown's best interests at heart.

183
00:16:10,730 --> 00:16:14,810
I see. And have you shared these suspicions with Lord Tywin?

184
00:16:15,830 --> 00:16:18,210
My father's a practical man. He appreciates facts.

185
00:16:18,210 --> 00:16:20,800
Myself, I often find them a hindrance.

186
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:24,110
And he appreciates those who aid his family, as you well know.

187
00:16:24,110 --> 00:16:25,920
He's almost as generous to those who help us

188
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:28,760
as he is unpleasant towards those who don't.

189
00:16:29,050 --> 00:16:31,580
You have a good working relationship with the Tyrells.

190
00:16:31,690 --> 00:16:34,170
I thought you might look into it before you leave the capital.

191
00:16:34,490 --> 00:16:36,620
- I shall do my best. - Thank you.

192
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:37,900
And your best will prove better than

193
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:40,430
when I asked you to locate Arya Stark?

194
00:16:40,430 --> 00:16:41,990
I assure you that it will.

195
00:16:49,170 --> 00:16:51,640
Gods, boy, that's enough. We're not in a tavern.

196
00:16:51,650 --> 00:16:52,880
- Pardon, my lady. - No need to speak.

197
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:54,950
Are there any figs? Fetch some.

198
00:16:55,410 --> 00:16:57,470
I always take figs midafternoon.

199
00:16:57,470 --> 00:16:59,060
They help move the bowels.

200
00:16:59,530 --> 00:17:01,050
To what do I owe this summons?

201
00:17:01,050 --> 00:17:02,900
Thank you for seeing me, my lady.

202
00:17:03,290 --> 00:17:05,340
I had hoped we might discuss a few financial matters.

203
00:17:05,340 --> 00:17:08,810
I climbed all those steps to discuss financial matters?

204
00:17:08,810 --> 00:17:10,160
It's the royal wedding.

205
00:17:10,620 --> 00:17:11,950
I'm told you had a hand in planning it.

206
00:17:11,950 --> 00:17:12,650
Naturally.

207
00:17:12,650 --> 00:17:15,600
It's shaping up to be a very involved affair.

208
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:17,610
The word extravagant has been used.

209
00:17:17,610 --> 00:17:19,020
What good is the word extravagant

210
00:17:19,020 --> 00:17:21,730
if it can't be used to describe a royal wedding?

211
00:17:21,730 --> 00:17:23,660
- I understand that. - Good.

212
00:17:24,010 --> 00:17:26,170
But, as Master of Coin, it falls upon me

213
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:27,770
to calculate the cost for the crown.

214
00:17:27,770 --> 00:17:30,280
As of now, it's a huge expense.

215
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:31,290
And?

216
00:17:32,450 --> 00:17:35,660
And we're at war, Lady Olenna.

217
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:37,510
Oh, I'd nearly forgotten.

218
00:17:37,510 --> 00:17:39,170
Yes, and maintaining supply lines--

219
00:17:39,170 --> 00:17:40,820
I can't think how it slipped my mind.

220
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:43,800
What is it, 12,000 infantrymen

221
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:45,730
the Tyrell family has supplied?

222
00:17:45,730 --> 00:17:47,970
1,800 mounted lances.

223
00:17:47,970 --> 00:17:49,950
2,000 in support.

224
00:17:49,950 --> 00:17:52,910
Provisions so this city might survive the winter.

225
00:17:52,910 --> 00:17:54,530
A million bushels of wheat.

226
00:17:54,530 --> 00:17:58,230
Half a million bushels each of barley, oats, and rye.

227
00:17:58,230 --> 00:18:00,210
20,000 head of cattle.

228
00:18:00,310 --> 00:18:01,620
50,000 sheep.

229
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:04,100
You don't have to lecture me about wartime expenses.

230
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:05,660
I'm quite familiar with them.

231
00:18:05,660 --> 00:18:07,670
And we are so grateful for your contributions

232
00:18:07,670 --> 00:18:10,470
which are necessary for the preservation of the realm.

233
00:18:10,470 --> 00:18:12,070
As is a royal wedding.

234
00:18:12,910 --> 00:18:14,940
The people are hungry for more than just food.

235
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:16,840
They crave distractions.

236
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:19,670
And if we don't provide them, they'll create their own.

237
00:18:20,010 --> 00:18:22,570
And their distractions are likely to end

238
00:18:22,570 --> 00:18:24,990
with us being torn to pieces.

239
00:18:25,110 --> 00:18:27,250
A royal wedding is much safer.

240
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:29,710
- Wouldn't you say? - I would.

241
00:18:30,650 --> 00:18:34,120
And traditionally paid for - by the royal family.

242
00:18:36,030 --> 00:18:38,170
I was told you were drunk, impertinent,

243
00:18:38,170 --> 00:18:40,210
and thoroughly debauched.

244
00:18:40,450 --> 00:18:41,840
You can imagine my disappointment

245
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:45,090
at finding nothing but a browbeaten bookkeeper.

246
00:18:46,620 --> 00:18:49,040
Where did you go for them, Volantis?

247
00:18:50,350 --> 00:18:51,990
- My lady-- - Oh, very well.

248
00:18:51,990 --> 00:18:54,220
I won't have it said that House Tyrell

249
00:18:54,220 --> 00:18:55,970
refuses to play its part.

250
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,320
We'll pay for half the expenses

251
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:59,790
and the celebrations will go on as planned.

252
00:19:00,450 --> 00:19:02,220
- Is that sufficient? - Quite sufficient. Thank you.

253
00:19:02,230 --> 00:19:04,660
Very good, then. That's settled. Good day.

254
00:19:08,090 --> 00:19:08,940
Give me that.

255
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:15,570
What are you doing?

256
00:19:17,790 --> 00:19:19,360
Just mending Lord Beric's armor.

257
00:19:19,810 --> 00:19:20,570
Why?

258
00:19:22,210 --> 00:19:24,460
I'm going to stay on and smith for the Brotherhood.

259
00:19:24,650 --> 00:19:25,920
Have you lost your mind?

260
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:27,610
When the Lannisters find this place,

261
00:19:27,610 --> 00:19:29,160
you think they'll spare the smiths?

262
00:19:29,950 --> 00:19:30,940
They'll cave your head in with your own helmet.

263
00:19:30,940 --> 00:19:33,820
The Lannisters wanted to kill me long before I joined the Brotherhood.

264
00:19:33,930 --> 00:19:35,140
You don't have to do this.

265
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:36,960
I want to.

266
00:19:38,330 --> 00:19:39,160
They need good men.

267
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:42,200
Robb needs good men, too. We're leaving tomorrow.

268
00:19:42,660 --> 00:19:44,630
- And then you-- - What? Serve him?

269
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:48,190
I've served men my entire life.

270
00:19:49,340 --> 00:19:50,640
I served Master Mott at King's Landing

271
00:19:50,650 --> 00:19:52,560
and he sold me to the Watch.

272
00:19:53,620 --> 00:19:54,660
I served Lord Tywin at Harrenhal,

273
00:19:54,660 --> 00:19:57,890
wondering every day if I'd get tortured or killed.

274
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:00,620
I'm done serving.

275
00:20:00,910 --> 00:20:02,780
You just said you were serving Lord Beric.

276
00:20:04,090 --> 00:20:06,740
He may be their leader, but they chose him.

277
00:20:08,090 --> 00:20:11,050
These men are brothers. They're a family.

278
00:20:12,910 --> 00:20:13,990
I've never had a family.

279
00:20:17,710 --> 00:20:18,990
I can be your family.

280
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:24,030
You wouldn't be my family.

281
00:20:25,540 --> 00:20:26,540
You'd be "My lady."

282
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:46,760
Willem.

283
00:20:50,560 --> 00:20:51,320
Willem!

284
00:20:54,660 --> 00:20:57,260
- Is this a rescue? - Lannister filth!

285
00:20:57,260 --> 00:20:59,290
- Take him! - Please, I didn't do anything.

286
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:01,300
I'm just a squire. Please

287
00:21:15,370 --> 00:21:16,200
Bring them in.

288
00:21:33,030 --> 00:21:33,890
Is that all of them?

289
00:21:37,280 --> 00:21:39,760
It took five of you to murder two unarmed squires?

290
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:41,480
Not murder, Your Grace.

291
00:21:42,170 --> 00:21:43,150
Vengeance.

292
00:21:43,150 --> 00:21:43,900
Vengeance?

293
00:21:46,010 --> 00:21:47,620
Those boys didn't kill your sons.

294
00:21:48,630 --> 00:21:51,120
I saw Harrion die on the battlefield and Torrhen--

295
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:53,220
Was strangled by the Kingslayer.

296
00:21:53,690 --> 00:21:55,340
- They were his kin. - They were boys!

297
00:21:58,070 --> 00:21:58,830
Look at them.

298
00:22:01,610 --> 00:22:02,910
Tell your mother to look at them.

299
00:22:03,460 --> 00:22:05,040
She killed them as much as I.

300
00:22:05,570 --> 00:22:07,650
My mother had nothing to do with this.

301
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:09,580
This was your treason.

302
00:22:09,580 --> 00:22:12,300
It's treason to free your enemies.

303
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:14,090
In war, you kill your enemies.

304
00:22:14,090 --> 00:22:16,330
Did your father not teach you that, boy?

305
00:22:16,990 --> 00:22:17,750
Leave him.

306
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:24,020
Aye.

307
00:22:25,460 --> 00:22:26,810
Leave me to the king.

308
00:22:27,070 --> 00:22:30,660
He wants to give me a scolding before he sets me free.

309
00:22:31,640 --> 00:22:34,590
That's how he deals with treason.

310
00:22:35,390 --> 00:22:37,330
Our King in the North.

311
00:22:37,810 --> 00:22:39,190
Or should I call him

312
00:22:40,070 --> 00:22:42,840
the King Who Lost the North?

313
00:22:45,910 --> 00:22:48,180
Escort Lord Karstark to the dungeon.

314
00:22:48,420 --> 00:22:49,450
Hang the rest.

315
00:22:49,530 --> 00:22:51,130
Mercy, sire! I didn't kill anyone.

316
00:22:51,130 --> 00:22:52,830
I only watched for the guards.

317
00:22:52,830 --> 00:22:54,390
This one was only the watcher.

318
00:22:55,200 --> 00:22:57,070
Hang him last so he can watch the others die.

319
00:22:57,150 --> 00:22:59,540
Please! Please, no. They made me do it!

320
00:22:59,830 --> 00:23:03,030
They made me! They made me!

321
00:23:11,670 --> 00:23:13,580
Word of this can't leave Riverrun.

322
00:23:14,170 --> 00:23:15,370
They were Tywin Lannister's nephews.

323
00:23:15,370 --> 00:23:17,200
The Lannisters pay their debts.

324
00:23:17,860 --> 00:23:18,790
They never stop talking about it.

325
00:23:18,790 --> 00:23:20,810
Would you make me a liar as well as a murderer?

326
00:23:21,010 --> 00:23:22,060
It wouldn't be lying.

327
00:23:22,850 --> 00:23:24,950
We will bury them and remain silent

328
00:23:25,140 --> 00:23:26,260
until the war is done.

329
00:23:26,290 --> 00:23:27,460
I'm not fighting for justice

330
00:23:27,460 --> 00:23:30,830
if I don't serve justice to murderers in my ranks,

331
00:23:30,830 --> 00:23:32,610
no matter how highborn.

332
00:23:34,730 --> 00:23:35,750
He has to die.

333
00:23:36,340 --> 00:23:38,320
The Karstarks are Northmen.

334
00:23:39,410 --> 00:23:41,030
They won't forgive the killing of their lord.

335
00:23:41,030 --> 00:23:42,290
Your mother's right.

336
00:23:43,700 --> 00:23:46,060
If you do this, the Karstarks will abandon you.

337
00:23:46,060 --> 00:23:47,880
You tended to their wounds.

338
00:23:48,660 --> 00:23:50,810
You brought them supper. Now they're dead.

339
00:23:50,810 --> 00:23:54,590
And more boys will keep dying until this war is over.

340
00:23:54,590 --> 00:23:56,800
You need Karstark men to end it.

341
00:23:57,050 --> 00:23:59,300
Spare his life. Keep him as a hostage.

342
00:23:59,620 --> 00:24:00,490
A hostage.

343
00:24:02,010 --> 00:24:04,640
Tell the Karstarks that as long as they remain loyal,

344
00:24:05,360 --> 00:24:06,520
he will not be harmed.

345
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:35,080
The blood of the First Men flows through my veins

346
00:24:35,080 --> 00:24:37,040
as much as yours, boy.

347
00:24:38,340 --> 00:24:40,620
I fought the Mad King for your father.

348
00:24:41,700 --> 00:24:43,310
I fought Joffrey for you.

349
00:24:44,690 --> 00:24:46,190
We are kin--

350
00:24:46,250 --> 00:24:48,670
Stark and Karstark.

351
00:24:48,690 --> 00:24:50,720
That didn't stop you from betraying me.

352
00:24:51,070 --> 00:24:52,430
And it won't save you now.

353
00:24:52,770 --> 00:24:54,690
I don't want it to save me.

354
00:24:55,720 --> 00:24:58,630
I want it to haunt you to the end of your days.

355
00:25:00,220 --> 00:25:01,610
Kneel, my lord.

356
00:25:11,070 --> 00:25:12,400
Rickard Karstark,

357
00:25:13,150 --> 00:25:14,340
Lord of Karhold,

358
00:25:15,100 --> 00:25:17,950
here in sight of gods and men, I sentence you to die.

359
00:25:19,220 --> 00:25:21,010
Would you speak a final word?

360
00:25:22,580 --> 00:25:24,570
Kill me and be cursed.

361
00:25:25,040 --> 00:25:27,210
You are no king of mine.

362
00:25:42,510 --> 00:25:43,290
Joffrey.

363
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:45,880
Cersei.

364
00:25:48,750 --> 00:25:49,700
Ilyn Payne.

365
00:25:52,200 --> 00:25:53,120
Ser Meryn.

366
00:25:57,450 --> 00:25:58,210
The Hound.

367
00:26:03,130 --> 00:26:04,170
What are you going to do with me?

368
00:26:04,840 --> 00:26:06,660
At first light we'll ride for Riverrun.

369
00:26:07,810 --> 00:26:08,960
Your brother's there now.

370
00:26:09,680 --> 00:26:11,580
He'll make a contribution to our cause

371
00:26:11,820 --> 00:26:13,070
and you can go home.

372
00:26:13,770 --> 00:26:16,190
I'm a hostage and you're selling me.

373
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:17,400
Don't think of it that way.

374
00:26:17,830 --> 00:26:19,940
- But it is that way. - It is.

375
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:23,290
- And it isn't. - More is than isn't.

376
00:26:25,480 --> 00:26:27,640
Beric admired your father a great deal, you know.

377
00:26:28,640 --> 00:26:30,350
He wanted to refuse your ransom altogether.

378
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:32,930
- So why don't you? - We need the gold.

379
00:26:46,220 --> 00:26:47,660
Do I frighten you, child?

380
00:26:48,120 --> 00:26:48,940
No.

381
00:26:52,900 --> 00:26:53,960
You're angry with me.

382
00:26:54,320 --> 00:26:55,370
And I don't blame you.

383
00:26:55,940 --> 00:26:57,530
But letting him go was the right thing.

384
00:26:58,100 --> 00:27:00,030
I have more reason than most to want him hanged.

385
00:27:00,030 --> 00:27:02,130
- I thought he killed you. - He did.

386
00:27:02,670 --> 00:27:03,560
But how...?

387
00:27:04,730 --> 00:27:05,600
Thoros...

388
00:27:06,770 --> 00:27:08,510
how many times have you brought me back?

389
00:27:09,140 --> 00:27:10,970
It's the Lord of Light brings you back.

390
00:27:12,470 --> 00:27:14,500
I'm just the lucky drunk who says the words.

391
00:27:14,660 --> 00:27:16,890
- How many times? - Five, I think.

392
00:27:17,160 --> 00:27:18,290
No, this makes six.

393
00:27:19,740 --> 00:27:23,140
- Six. - There was the first time-- the Mountain.

394
00:27:24,010 --> 00:27:24,780
Show her.

395
00:27:25,620 --> 00:27:28,170
Lance right through the chest.

396
00:27:29,220 --> 00:27:31,300
Then I was stabbed in the belly.

397
00:27:31,300 --> 00:27:33,000
Then it was an arrow in the back.

398
00:27:33,320 --> 00:27:34,790
And that axe in the side.

399
00:27:35,680 --> 00:27:38,620
Then the Lannisters caught me and executed me for treason.

400
00:27:40,760 --> 00:27:42,750
Was it a hanging or a dagger in the eye?

401
00:27:42,750 --> 00:27:45,680
Both. Fuckers couldn't decide.

402
00:27:46,840 --> 00:27:48,270
And the Hound makes six.

403
00:27:48,920 --> 00:27:50,750
Second time I've been killed by a Clegane.

404
00:27:50,770 --> 00:27:51,890
You'd think you'd learn.

405
00:27:54,180 --> 00:27:55,980
It's not getting any easier, you know.

406
00:27:57,470 --> 00:27:58,230
I know.

407
00:27:59,060 --> 00:28:00,420
Every time I come back,

408
00:28:02,110 --> 00:28:03,000
I'm a bit less.

409
00:28:05,100 --> 00:28:06,700
Pieces of you get chipped away.

410
00:28:09,150 --> 00:28:10,910
Could you bring back a man without a head?

411
00:28:13,220 --> 00:28:16,610
Not six times. Just once.

412
00:28:17,890 --> 00:28:19,690
I don't think it works that way, child.

413
00:28:24,760 --> 00:28:27,400
He was a good man, Ned Stark.

414
00:28:28,740 --> 00:28:31,550
He's at rest now, somewhere.

415
00:28:32,020 --> 00:28:34,000
I would never wish my life upon him.

416
00:28:34,870 --> 00:28:36,170
I would.

417
00:28:39,410 --> 00:28:40,800
You're alive.

418
00:28:46,250 --> 00:28:49,020
Lord, cast your light upon me.

419
00:28:49,950 --> 00:28:52,760
Protect me in the darkness.

420
00:28:53,640 --> 00:28:56,080
Burn away my sins.

421
00:28:57,190 --> 00:28:59,910
Help me serve you.

422
00:29:00,510 --> 00:29:02,660
Use me as you will.

423
00:29:05,040 --> 00:29:06,880
For the night is dark

424
00:29:07,690 --> 00:29:09,440
and full of terrors.

425
00:29:20,890 --> 00:29:24,400
I have prayed day and night for you to come to me.

426
00:29:25,940 --> 00:29:27,090
My lady.

427
00:29:27,880 --> 00:29:29,480
I meant to come sooner.

428
00:29:30,770 --> 00:29:33,490
- The battle-- - I know of your troubles, my king.

429
00:29:33,950 --> 00:29:36,690
The Lady Melisandre has told me everything.

430
00:29:37,490 --> 00:29:39,070
Yes, of course.

431
00:29:48,180 --> 00:29:51,990
You mustn't despair. Your claim is true.

432
00:29:51,990 --> 00:29:54,780
- You will be victorious. - I believed that once.

433
00:29:54,790 --> 00:29:57,370
You are the one god's champion

434
00:29:58,110 --> 00:30:00,490
and the finest man I've ever known.

435
00:30:00,490 --> 00:30:01,870
Selyse.

436
00:30:04,310 --> 00:30:06,370
I've broken a sacred vow.

437
00:30:10,520 --> 00:30:11,750
I've sinned.

438
00:30:11,750 --> 00:30:14,130
- No. - I've wronged you.

439
00:30:14,900 --> 00:30:18,300
- I have shamed you. - You're doing god's work.

440
00:30:18,300 --> 00:30:19,740
You don't understand.

441
00:30:26,190 --> 00:30:27,550
The Red Woman--

442
00:30:30,370 --> 00:30:31,560
The Lady Melisandre--

443
00:30:31,560 --> 00:30:33,170
I know, Stannis.

444
00:30:34,050 --> 00:30:37,360
The Lady Melisandre has told me everything.

445
00:30:37,730 --> 00:30:41,100
No act done in service of the Lord of Light

446
00:30:41,100 --> 00:30:42,640
can ever be a sin.

447
00:30:43,430 --> 00:30:46,350
When she told me,

448
00:30:47,080 --> 00:30:51,100
I wept with joy.

449
00:31:01,880 --> 00:31:05,280
Oh, my sweet boys.

450
00:31:07,010 --> 00:31:09,890
Petyr, Tommard,

451
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:12,280
Edric.

452
00:31:14,130 --> 00:31:17,580
I thank god every day

453
00:31:17,580 --> 00:31:20,070
for bringing Melisandre to us.

454
00:31:20,300 --> 00:31:23,000
She gave you a son.

455
00:31:23,990 --> 00:31:26,940
I gave you...

456
00:31:28,570 --> 00:31:30,710
- nothing. - That's not true.

457
00:31:35,480 --> 00:31:37,580
So you've come to see her as well?

458
00:31:40,460 --> 00:31:42,160
There is no need.

459
00:31:43,910 --> 00:31:46,740
You must keep away from such distractions.

460
00:31:46,740 --> 00:31:48,250
She's my daughter.

461
00:31:50,170 --> 00:31:51,810
I want to see her.

462
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:55,810
You are a king.

463
00:31:57,170 --> 00:31:59,170
You don't need my permission.

464
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:06,310
*Under the sea*

465
00:32:06,580 --> 00:32:09,350
*I know, I know*

466
00:32:12,300 --> 00:32:15,440
*The birds have scales*

467
00:32:15,440 --> 00:32:18,240
*And the fish take wing*

468
00:32:18,250 --> 00:32:21,050
*I know, I know*

469
00:32:21,250 --> 00:32:23,650
*Oh, oh, oh*

470
00:32:24,440 --> 00:32:25,640
Shireen.

471
00:32:25,750 --> 00:32:26,970
Father!

472
00:32:35,610 --> 00:32:37,670
You've grown since I last saw you.

473
00:32:37,920 --> 00:32:40,080
Mother said you fought in a battle.

474
00:32:41,380 --> 00:32:42,700
Did you win?

475
00:32:44,130 --> 00:32:45,240
No.

476
00:32:46,600 --> 00:32:48,680
Did the Onion Knight come back with you?

477
00:32:49,950 --> 00:32:51,370
He did.

478
00:32:52,120 --> 00:32:53,820
He fought bravely.

479
00:32:53,820 --> 00:32:55,640
He hasn't come to visit me.

480
00:32:55,800 --> 00:32:58,480
He said he'd bring me back a present from the capital.

481
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:00,220
He won't be visiting, child.

482
00:33:00,220 --> 00:33:02,520
Why not? He's my friend.

483
00:33:02,520 --> 00:33:03,540
Look.

484
00:33:11,870 --> 00:33:13,520
He made this for me.

485
00:33:14,150 --> 00:33:15,900
But don't tell Mother I have it.

486
00:33:16,380 --> 00:33:17,960
It's a secret.

487
00:33:17,960 --> 00:33:20,130
Mother doesn't like the Onion Knight.

488
00:33:22,800 --> 00:33:25,200
Ser Davos is a traitor.

489
00:33:26,820 --> 00:33:30,170
He's rotting in a dungeon cell for his crime.

490
00:33:39,630 --> 00:33:41,190
Best forget him.

491
00:33:53,420 --> 00:33:56,540
Not so hard. You'll scrub the skin off.

492
00:33:56,540 --> 00:33:57,830
What are you doing here?

493
00:33:57,830 --> 00:33:59,290
I need a bath.

494
00:33:59,850 --> 00:34:01,820
Help me out of these rags.

495
00:34:08,990 --> 00:34:10,530
Now get out.

496
00:34:24,020 --> 00:34:25,740
There's another tub.

497
00:34:26,460 --> 00:34:28,570
This one suits me fine.

498
00:34:41,230 --> 00:34:43,940
Don't worry. I'm not interested.

499
00:34:46,240 --> 00:34:48,540
If I faint, pull me out.

500
00:34:48,960 --> 00:34:52,440
I don't intend to be the first Lannister to die in a bathtub.

501
00:34:52,450 --> 00:34:54,110
Why should I care how you die?

502
00:34:54,110 --> 00:34:56,770
You swore a solemn vow, remember?

503
00:34:57,380 --> 00:35:00,630
You're supposed to get me to King's Landing in one piece.

504
00:35:01,550 --> 00:35:03,970
Not going so well, is it?

505
00:35:04,560 --> 00:35:07,100
No wonder Renly died with you guarding him.

506
00:35:16,870 --> 00:35:19,020
That was unworthy. Forgive me.

507
00:35:19,500 --> 00:35:21,040
You protected me better than most--

508
00:35:21,050 --> 00:35:23,640
- Don't you mock me. - I'm apologizing.

509
00:35:25,630 --> 00:35:27,300
I'm sick of fighting.

510
00:35:27,960 --> 00:35:29,240
Let's call a truce.

511
00:35:29,240 --> 00:35:31,310
You need trust to have a truce.

512
00:35:32,590 --> 00:35:34,160
I trust you.

513
00:35:41,690 --> 00:35:44,710
There it is. There's the look.

514
00:35:45,230 --> 00:35:47,120
I've seen it for 17 years

515
00:35:47,120 --> 00:35:49,010
on face after face.

516
00:35:49,530 --> 00:35:51,530
You all despise me.

517
00:35:51,760 --> 00:35:53,410
Kingslayer.

518
00:35:53,740 --> 00:35:55,360
Oathbreaker.

519
00:35:56,470 --> 00:35:58,220
A man without honor.

520
00:36:04,800 --> 00:36:06,340
You've heard of wildfire?

521
00:36:06,760 --> 00:36:07,710
Of course.

522
00:36:07,710 --> 00:36:09,720
The Mad King was obsessed with it.

523
00:36:10,300 --> 00:36:12,520
He loved to watch people burn,

524
00:36:13,380 --> 00:36:16,180
the way their skin blackened and blistered

525
00:36:16,180 --> 00:36:18,120
and melted off their bones.

526
00:36:18,190 --> 00:36:20,650
He burned lords he didn't like.

527
00:36:20,650 --> 00:36:22,730
He burned Hands who disobeyed him.

528
00:36:22,730 --> 00:36:25,770
He burned anyone who was against him.

529
00:36:27,680 --> 00:36:30,440
Before long, half the country was against him.

530
00:36:33,670 --> 00:36:36,020
Aerys saw traitors everywhere.

531
00:36:37,480 --> 00:36:43,410
So he had his pyromancer place caches of wildfire all over the city--

532
00:36:44,280 --> 00:36:46,230
beneath the Sept of Baelor

533
00:36:46,430 --> 00:36:48,180
and the slums of Flea Bottom.

534
00:36:48,180 --> 00:36:51,690
Under houses, stables, taverns.

535
00:36:51,810 --> 00:36:54,140
Even beneath the Red Keep itself.

536
00:36:56,680 --> 00:36:58,050
Finally,

537
00:36:59,360 --> 00:37:01,740
the day of reckoning came.

538
00:37:02,370 --> 00:37:04,650
Robert Baratheon marched on the capital

539
00:37:04,650 --> 00:37:06,590
after his victory at the Trident.

540
00:37:06,970 --> 00:37:09,100
But my father arrived first

541
00:37:09,460 --> 00:37:11,890
with the whole Lannister army at his back,

542
00:37:12,150 --> 00:37:16,480
promising to defend the city against the rebels.

543
00:37:18,550 --> 00:37:20,600
I knew my father better than that.

544
00:37:20,620 --> 00:37:23,410
He's never been one to pick the losing side.

545
00:37:23,970 --> 00:37:26,040
I told the Mad King as much.

546
00:37:26,540 --> 00:37:29,760
I urged him to surrender peacefully.

547
00:37:30,580 --> 00:37:32,680
But the king didn't listen to me.

548
00:37:33,430 --> 00:37:36,040
He didn't listen to Varys who tried to warn him.

549
00:37:36,060 --> 00:37:40,140
But he did listen to Grand Maester Pycelle,

550
00:37:40,790 --> 00:37:42,880
that grey, sunken cunt.

551
00:37:44,680 --> 00:37:47,280
"You can trust the Lannisters," He said.

552
00:37:49,280 --> 00:37:51,010
"The Lannisters have always been

553
00:37:51,350 --> 00:37:53,570
true friends of the crown."

554
00:37:55,940 --> 00:37:58,970
So we opened the gates

555
00:37:58,970 --> 00:38:00,900
and my father sacked the city.

556
00:38:01,640 --> 00:38:04,300
Once again, I came to the king,

557
00:38:04,390 --> 00:38:07,340
begging him to surrender.

558
00:38:11,240 --> 00:38:12,860
He told me to...

559
00:38:13,650 --> 00:38:16,040
bring him my father's head.

560
00:38:17,550 --> 00:38:18,910
Then he...

561
00:38:19,560 --> 00:38:21,640
turned to his pyromancer.

562
00:38:22,920 --> 00:38:25,080
"Burn them all," He said.

563
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:29,470
"Burn them in their homes.

564
00:38:29,470 --> 00:38:31,190
Burn them in their beds."

565
00:38:32,930 --> 00:38:36,980
Tell me, if your precious Renly

566
00:38:37,810 --> 00:38:40,730
commanded you to kill your own father

567
00:38:40,730 --> 00:38:43,490
and stand by while thousands of men,

568
00:38:43,920 --> 00:38:45,880
women, and children burned alive,

569
00:38:45,880 --> 00:38:47,590
would you have done it?

570
00:38:48,830 --> 00:38:50,780
Would you have kept your oath then?

571
00:38:54,650 --> 00:38:58,430
First, I killed the pyromancer.

572
00:38:58,430 --> 00:39:01,940
And then when the king turned to flee,

573
00:39:01,950 --> 00:39:05,400
I drove my sword into his back.

574
00:39:06,300 --> 00:39:08,190
"Burn them all," He kept saying.

575
00:39:09,140 --> 00:39:10,840
"Burn them all."

576
00:39:11,070 --> 00:39:13,500
I don't think he expected to die.

577
00:39:13,500 --> 00:39:16,240
He-- he meant to...

578
00:39:17,820 --> 00:39:19,400
burn with the rest of us

579
00:39:19,400 --> 00:39:22,440
and rise again,

580
00:39:23,190 --> 00:39:25,090
reborn as a dragon

581
00:39:25,090 --> 00:39:27,080
to turn his enemies to ash.

582
00:39:30,870 --> 00:39:34,230
I slit his throat to make sure that didn't happen.

583
00:39:38,370 --> 00:39:41,150
That's where Ned Stark found me.

584
00:39:42,990 --> 00:39:44,740
If this is true...

585
00:39:45,760 --> 00:39:47,680
why didn't you tell anyone?

586
00:39:49,630 --> 00:39:51,740
Why didn't you tell Lord Stark?

587
00:39:51,740 --> 00:39:52,870
Stark?

588
00:39:53,300 --> 00:39:54,410
You think

589
00:39:55,650 --> 00:39:59,580
the honorable Ned Stark

590
00:40:00,020 --> 00:40:02,250
wanted to hear my side?

591
00:40:03,220 --> 00:40:05,860
He judged me guilty

592
00:40:05,860 --> 00:40:07,940
the moment he set eyes on me.

593
00:40:12,250 --> 00:40:15,290
By what right does the wolf

594
00:40:15,290 --> 00:40:16,890
judge the lion?

595
00:40:18,490 --> 00:40:20,460
- By what right? - Help! Help!

596
00:40:20,460 --> 00:40:22,030
The Kingslayer!

597
00:40:23,310 --> 00:40:24,750
Jaime.

598
00:40:25,070 --> 00:40:27,130
My name is Jaime.

599
00:40:30,940 --> 00:40:32,420
Onion Knight.

600
00:40:32,920 --> 00:40:34,550
Ser Onion Knight.

601
00:40:35,720 --> 00:40:38,510
Princess? Gods, what are you doing here?

602
00:40:38,510 --> 00:40:40,960
- Shh, you'll wake Bert. - Bert?

603
00:40:41,030 --> 00:40:44,130
He's the fat one. He's on guard duty tonight.

604
00:40:44,130 --> 00:40:46,400
He likes to drink wine and sleep a lot.

605
00:40:46,400 --> 00:40:48,610
Go back to your room. You're not supposed to be here.

606
00:40:48,720 --> 00:40:50,950
- If your father knew-- - He said you were a traitor.

607
00:40:51,500 --> 00:40:52,560
Are you?

608
00:40:53,420 --> 00:40:54,800
I am, child.

609
00:40:55,990 --> 00:40:57,580
I disobeyed my king, your father,

610
00:40:57,580 --> 00:40:59,480
and now I'm paying the price.

611
00:41:00,270 --> 00:41:02,150
I don't care. You're my friend.

612
00:41:02,250 --> 00:41:03,910
You must get bored down here.

613
00:41:03,920 --> 00:41:05,650
I brought you something to read.

614
00:41:05,920 --> 00:41:07,960
It's about Aegon and his dragons.

615
00:41:08,330 --> 00:41:10,890
Aegon used to live here. Did you know that?

616
00:41:10,890 --> 00:41:13,130
- And the Targaryens built this castle. - Aye.

617
00:41:13,130 --> 00:41:15,640
- So they did. - You can hide the book under your cloak.

618
00:41:15,680 --> 00:41:17,730
It's a good one. I'll bring you more.

619
00:41:17,730 --> 00:41:20,270
Thank you, my lady. I'm sure it's a fine book,

620
00:41:20,870 --> 00:41:22,300
but it's wasted on me.

621
00:41:22,300 --> 00:41:23,970
Take it. I have more.

622
00:41:25,860 --> 00:41:27,540
My lady, I can't read the words.

623
00:41:28,280 --> 00:41:29,760
You can't?

624
00:41:30,500 --> 00:41:33,200
I'll teach you. I'll come when Bert's on duty and teach you.

625
00:41:33,200 --> 00:41:35,140
- No. No. No. - It's easy. It'll be fun.

626
00:41:35,140 --> 00:41:37,130
- Go. We can't. - Why not?

627
00:41:37,130 --> 00:41:40,230
What will they do, lock us in cells?

628
00:41:46,470 --> 00:41:47,790
I wouldn't know where to start.

629
00:41:47,790 --> 00:41:49,170
At the beginning.

630
00:41:49,980 --> 00:41:51,600
This word is Aegon.

631
00:41:51,670 --> 00:41:55,910
When you see A, E, and G together like that,

632
00:41:56,050 --> 00:41:57,660
it sounds like egg.

633
00:41:57,910 --> 00:41:59,670
And the title of the whole book

634
00:41:59,670 --> 00:42:04,060
is "An History of Aegon the Conqueror and His Conquest of Westeros."

635
00:42:16,400 --> 00:42:17,930
It was a bitch of a siege.

636
00:42:17,940 --> 00:42:20,280
Mm, you were first through the breach at Pyke?

637
00:42:20,340 --> 00:42:23,600
The second. Thoros of Myr went in alone,

638
00:42:23,600 --> 00:42:25,910
waving that flaming sword of his.

639
00:42:25,910 --> 00:42:28,450
Thoros of Myr. Bloody madman.

640
00:42:28,720 --> 00:42:30,760
Robert knighted you after the battle?

641
00:42:31,800 --> 00:42:33,520
Proudest moment of my life.

642
00:42:33,520 --> 00:42:36,510
One knee in the dust, the king's sword on my shoulder,

643
00:42:36,640 --> 00:42:37,780
listening to the words.

644
00:42:37,780 --> 00:42:40,610
"In the name of the Warrior, I charge you to be brave."

645
00:42:42,010 --> 00:42:44,720
All I could think of was how badly I had to piss.

646
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:48,780
In full plate metal for 16 hours.

647
00:42:48,810 --> 00:42:50,800
Never occurred to me till the fighting was over.

648
00:42:50,800 --> 00:42:52,110
I was very nearly the first

649
00:42:52,110 --> 00:42:54,080
man knighted to piss on the king's boots.

650
00:42:55,720 --> 00:42:57,160
Robert would have laughed.

651
00:42:58,290 --> 00:43:00,490
He was a good man, a great warrior.

652
00:43:02,590 --> 00:43:04,310
And a terrible king.

653
00:43:04,410 --> 00:43:07,620
I burned away my years fighting for terrible kings.

654
00:43:07,620 --> 00:43:09,600
- You swore an oath. - Yes.

655
00:43:09,600 --> 00:43:11,400
And a man of honor keeps his vows,

656
00:43:11,730 --> 00:43:14,490
even if he's serving a drunk or a lunatic.

657
00:43:14,620 --> 00:43:17,040
Just once in my life before it's over,

658
00:43:17,740 --> 00:43:20,080
I want to know what it's like to serve with pride,

659
00:43:20,700 --> 00:43:22,470
to fight for someone I believe in.

660
00:43:23,480 --> 00:43:24,840
Do you believe in her?

661
00:43:28,210 --> 00:43:29,600
With all my heart.

662
00:43:35,330 --> 00:43:36,480
These are the ones?

663
00:43:36,480 --> 00:43:38,260
Yes, khaleesi. The officers.

664
00:44:14,510 --> 00:44:16,610
All Unsullied boys are given new names

665
00:44:16,610 --> 00:44:18,110
when they are cut--

666
00:44:18,260 --> 00:44:21,170
Grey Worm, Red Flea, Black Rat.

667
00:44:21,170 --> 00:44:23,760
Names that remind them what they are--

668
00:44:24,870 --> 00:44:26,020
vermin.

669
00:45:13,770 --> 00:45:15,350
King Robert wanted her dead.

670
00:45:15,470 --> 00:45:16,860
Of course he wanted her dead.

671
00:45:16,870 --> 00:45:19,170
She's a Targaryen. The last Targaryen.

672
00:45:20,440 --> 00:45:23,130
I suppose no one on the small council could speak sense to him.

673
00:45:23,130 --> 00:45:25,630
- I didn't sit on the small council. - No?

674
00:45:26,050 --> 00:45:28,570
Doesn't the Lord Commander of the Kingsguard traditionally--

675
00:45:28,580 --> 00:45:30,730
Traditionally, yes, but I killed a dozen

676
00:45:30,730 --> 00:45:32,560
of Robert's friends during his rebellion.

677
00:45:34,920 --> 00:45:36,530
He didn't want advice on how to govern

678
00:45:36,530 --> 00:45:38,750
from a man who had fought for the Mad King.

679
00:45:38,930 --> 00:45:40,550
Can't say I minded much.

680
00:45:41,490 --> 00:45:43,190
I always hated the politics.

681
00:45:43,900 --> 00:45:45,710
Yeah, I imagine I would, too.

682
00:45:45,730 --> 00:45:48,090
Hours spent jabbering about backstabbings

683
00:45:48,100 --> 00:45:50,580
and betrayals the world over.

684
00:45:54,680 --> 00:45:56,400
Still, she'll have to wade through that muck

685
00:45:56,400 --> 00:45:58,220
if she wants to rule the Seven Kingdoms.

686
00:45:58,640 --> 00:46:00,610
She'll have good men around her to advise her,

687
00:46:00,610 --> 00:46:02,100
men with experience.

688
00:46:02,370 --> 00:46:03,800
Which men do you have in mind?

689
00:46:03,800 --> 00:46:06,030
Forgive me, Ser Jorah, for what I'm about to say,

690
00:46:06,730 --> 00:46:09,630
but your reputation in Westeros has suffered over the years.

691
00:46:10,040 --> 00:46:11,690
It suffered for a reason.

692
00:46:11,750 --> 00:46:13,690
I sold men into slavery.

693
00:46:13,730 --> 00:46:15,530
I don't know if your presence by her side

694
00:46:15,530 --> 00:46:17,800
will help our cause when we go home.

695
00:46:17,850 --> 00:46:19,060
Our cause?

696
00:46:19,850 --> 00:46:21,660
Forgive me, Ser Barristan, but I was busy

697
00:46:21,660 --> 00:46:23,840
defending the khaleesi against King Robert's assassins

698
00:46:23,840 --> 00:46:25,670
while you were still bowing to the man.

699
00:46:25,770 --> 00:46:28,660
We both want her to rule. Am I wrong?

700
00:46:29,690 --> 00:46:31,390
You only joined us a few days ago.

701
00:46:31,390 --> 00:46:33,090
I can't speak to your intentions.

702
00:46:33,190 --> 00:46:35,260
If we're truly her loyal servants,

703
00:46:35,890 --> 00:46:37,750
we will do whatever needs to be done,

704
00:46:38,430 --> 00:46:41,180
no matter the cost, no matter our pride.

705
00:46:41,180 --> 00:46:42,920
You're not Lord Commander here.

706
00:46:43,890 --> 00:46:45,590
You're just another exile.

707
00:46:46,500 --> 00:46:48,530
And I take my orders from the queen.

708
00:46:56,930 --> 00:46:59,610
- Come to bed. - You were right.

709
00:47:00,700 --> 00:47:02,370
The Karstarks are gone.

710
00:47:03,160 --> 00:47:05,080
Almost half our forces.

711
00:47:05,710 --> 00:47:09,020
Tywin Lannister knows what he needs to do to make us unravel.

712
00:47:10,080 --> 00:47:11,310
Nothing.

713
00:47:12,250 --> 00:47:13,600
Only wait.

714
00:47:14,550 --> 00:47:15,790
Don't let him.

715
00:47:16,960 --> 00:47:18,260
What can I do?

716
00:47:19,250 --> 00:47:20,770
Attack King's Landing?

717
00:47:20,980 --> 00:47:22,610
There's nothing he'd like better.

718
00:47:22,900 --> 00:47:24,580
He'd crush us in a day.

719
00:47:25,770 --> 00:47:27,350
We could ride north.

720
00:47:27,470 --> 00:47:29,490
Take your land back from the Greyjoys.

721
00:47:29,490 --> 00:47:32,880
- Wait out the winter. - Winter could last five years.

722
00:47:32,880 --> 00:47:34,570
Once my bannermen are home again,

723
00:47:34,570 --> 00:47:37,120
sitting by the fire, surrounded by their families,

724
00:47:37,120 --> 00:47:40,260
warm and safe, they'll never ride south again.

725
00:47:40,810 --> 00:47:42,290
When I gathered my lords together,

726
00:47:42,290 --> 00:47:44,180
we had a purpose, a mission.

727
00:47:44,190 --> 00:47:46,670
Now we're like a band of bickering children.

728
00:47:49,270 --> 00:47:51,010
Give them a new purpose.

729
00:47:51,280 --> 00:47:52,420
What?

730
00:47:54,700 --> 00:47:56,660
Oh, I don't know.

731
00:47:56,780 --> 00:47:58,860
I don't even know where Winterfell is.

732
00:48:02,160 --> 00:48:03,220
Here.

733
00:48:07,580 --> 00:48:10,600
And we're here. King's Landing--

734
00:48:17,580 --> 00:48:18,760
What is it?

735
00:48:22,350 --> 00:48:25,020
I can't force them to meet us in the field

736
00:48:25,680 --> 00:48:28,320
and I can't attack them where they're strongest,

737
00:48:28,450 --> 00:48:30,780
but I can attack them where they're not.

738
00:48:31,970 --> 00:48:34,170
And Casterly Rock can't run away.

739
00:48:36,630 --> 00:48:38,900
I'm going to take their home away from them.

740
00:48:40,630 --> 00:48:41,680
Can you do it?

741
00:48:42,820 --> 00:48:45,660
I need men to replace the Karstarks who marched home.

742
00:48:46,610 --> 00:48:48,020
There is only one person in this kingdom

743
00:48:48,020 --> 00:48:49,100
with that kind of army

744
00:48:49,100 --> 00:48:51,360
who hasn't already sided with the Lannisters.

745
00:48:53,350 --> 00:48:55,380
The man whose daughter I was supposed to marry--

746
00:48:56,970 --> 00:48:57,910
Walder Frey.

747
00:49:07,880 --> 00:49:09,760
He's such a splendid fighter.

748
00:49:10,540 --> 00:49:13,110
Do you have any idea when we might...

749
00:49:14,340 --> 00:49:16,690
I'll plant the seed as soon as Joffrey and I are married.

750
00:49:16,740 --> 00:49:17,920
It should grow quickly.

751
00:49:18,500 --> 00:49:19,490
Joffrey won't let me leave.

752
00:49:19,490 --> 00:49:22,320
He's got too many reasons to keep me here.

753
00:49:23,030 --> 00:49:24,860
And only one to let you go.

754
00:49:26,710 --> 00:49:28,270
Because it will please me.

755
00:49:28,800 --> 00:49:29,520
Squire!

756
00:49:34,240 --> 00:49:35,010
Well fought, ser.

757
00:49:35,550 --> 00:49:38,170
That was no fight. I don't know you.

758
00:49:38,800 --> 00:49:40,770
Olyver, if it please you.

759
00:49:43,360 --> 00:49:45,750
I should like to see you spar with a proper partner, ser.

760
00:49:54,300 --> 00:49:55,110
How did you know?

761
00:49:55,670 --> 00:49:56,490
Know what?

762
00:49:58,960 --> 00:49:59,970
That I wanted to.

763
00:50:00,800 --> 00:50:01,550
My lord...

764
00:50:06,970 --> 00:50:07,960
I'll have you know I'm to be married soon

765
00:50:07,960 --> 00:50:10,290
and even my intended hasn't the slightest notion.

766
00:50:11,590 --> 00:50:13,300
They rarely do, in my experience.

767
00:50:14,770 --> 00:50:16,770
You have a good deal of experience, do you?

768
00:50:18,040 --> 00:50:19,080
With the husbands.

769
00:50:29,020 --> 00:50:30,420
That didn't take long.

770
00:50:31,720 --> 00:50:32,950
Well, it took long enough.

771
00:50:35,010 --> 00:50:38,000
It seems our Knight of Flowers is engaged to be wed.

772
00:50:38,200 --> 00:50:39,030
Is he?

773
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:40,980
And...

774
00:50:42,170 --> 00:50:43,400
who's the lucky girl?

775
00:50:44,520 --> 00:50:46,630
She may not be the grandest ship in the world

776
00:50:47,680 --> 00:50:48,740
or the fastest,

777
00:50:50,810 --> 00:50:51,720
but she's mine.

778
00:50:55,830 --> 00:50:57,050
I've always wanted a ship.

779
00:50:57,720 --> 00:50:58,910
Now I want a dozen.

780
00:51:00,050 --> 00:51:02,200
- Strange, isn't it? - What is?

781
00:51:02,210 --> 00:51:04,250
It doesn't matter what we want,

782
00:51:04,640 --> 00:51:05,860
once we get it,

783
00:51:06,410 --> 00:51:07,880
then we want something else.

784
00:51:11,210 --> 00:51:13,720
Your hair is different.

785
00:51:14,010 --> 00:51:14,760
Is it?

786
00:51:15,870 --> 00:51:17,370
Lady Margaery wears it that way.

787
00:51:17,370 --> 00:51:19,080
Many ladies wear it this way.

788
00:51:20,200 --> 00:51:21,420
I have good news.

789
00:51:21,600 --> 00:51:23,100
I'll be leaving the city soon.

790
00:51:23,730 --> 00:51:24,750
You still want me to come with you?

791
00:51:24,750 --> 00:51:26,820
It's not a question of what I want.

792
00:51:27,460 --> 00:51:28,490
It's what you want.

793
00:51:29,500 --> 00:51:30,900
You want to go home, don't you?

794
00:51:30,980 --> 00:51:32,680
Of course. More than anything.

795
00:51:35,510 --> 00:51:38,680
But maybe it would be better to wait.

796
00:51:39,620 --> 00:51:41,890
I've been thinking how dangerous it would be.

797
00:51:41,890 --> 00:51:43,570
Not just for me, but for you.

798
00:51:44,880 --> 00:51:45,520
You've been so kind.

799
00:51:45,530 --> 00:51:48,320
I'd feel terrible if anything happened to you.

800
00:51:49,740 --> 00:51:51,880
I can't tell you how touched I am

801
00:51:52,290 --> 00:51:54,190
by your concern for my welfare.

802
00:51:55,760 --> 00:51:58,410
I hope you know that I'm your friend, Sansa.

803
00:51:59,240 --> 00:52:00,350
Your true friend.

804
00:52:00,960 --> 00:52:02,310
I do, Lord Baelish.

805
00:52:02,310 --> 00:52:03,890
- Petyr. - Petyr.

806
00:52:04,990 --> 00:52:06,430
If you wish to stay,

807
00:52:07,130 --> 00:52:09,470
then of course you will stay.

808
00:52:15,060 --> 00:52:17,010
We'll speak again when I return.

809
00:52:30,660 --> 00:52:31,550
You're late.

810
00:52:33,080 --> 00:52:34,870
What's she doing here?

811
00:52:35,410 --> 00:52:37,510
Our business concerns her, too.

812
00:52:37,690 --> 00:52:38,390
Sit.

813
00:52:41,300 --> 00:52:42,870
You'll be pleased to learn

814
00:52:42,870 --> 00:52:46,140
that after one conversation with Olenna Tyrell,

815
00:52:46,660 --> 00:52:47,660
I've saved the crown

816
00:52:47,660 --> 00:52:50,700
hundreds of thousands on this wedding.

817
00:52:50,840 --> 00:52:51,500
Never mind that now.

818
00:52:51,500 --> 00:52:53,290
We have something important to discuss.

819
00:52:53,290 --> 00:52:56,010
I'm Master of Coin. Saving money is important.

820
00:52:57,020 --> 00:52:57,940
Stop that.

821
00:52:58,590 --> 00:53:00,250
You're making me uncomfortable.

822
00:53:00,250 --> 00:53:02,890
Your sister has learned that your new friends the Tyrells

823
00:53:02,890 --> 00:53:06,440
are plotting to marry Sansa Stark to Ser Loras.

824
00:53:06,800 --> 00:53:07,560
Very well.

825
00:53:08,130 --> 00:53:09,100
She's a lovely girl.

826
00:53:10,380 --> 00:53:12,090
Missing some of Loras' favorite bits,

827
00:53:12,090 --> 00:53:13,830
but I'm sure they'll make do.

828
00:53:14,000 --> 00:53:16,260
- Your jokes are not appreciated. - It wasn't my best, but--

829
00:53:16,260 --> 00:53:19,510
I bring them into the royal fold and this is how they repay me,

830
00:53:19,510 --> 00:53:23,110
by trying to steal the key to the North out from under me.

831
00:53:23,120 --> 00:53:24,950
Sansa is the key to the North?

832
00:53:25,230 --> 00:53:26,940
I seem to remember she has an older brother.

833
00:53:26,950 --> 00:53:29,120
The Karstarks have marched home.

834
00:53:29,120 --> 00:53:30,910
The young wolf has lost half his army.

835
00:53:30,910 --> 00:53:32,400
His days are numbered.

836
00:53:32,690 --> 00:53:35,340
Theon Greyjoy murdered both his brothers.

837
00:53:35,350 --> 00:53:38,520
That makes Sansa Stark the heir to Winterfell.

838
00:53:39,280 --> 00:53:42,580
And I am not about to hand her over to the Tyrells.

839
00:53:42,580 --> 00:53:45,140
The Tyrell army is helping us to win this war.

840
00:53:45,450 --> 00:53:47,250
Do you really think it's wise to refuse them?

841
00:53:47,250 --> 00:53:49,790
There's nothing to refuse. This is a plot.

842
00:53:50,290 --> 00:53:52,200
Plots are not public knowledge.

843
00:53:52,520 --> 00:53:55,940
And the Tyrells won't carry this one out until after Joffrey's wedding.

844
00:53:56,570 --> 00:54:00,230
We need to act first and kill this union in its crib.

845
00:54:00,410 --> 00:54:01,670
And how do we do that?

846
00:54:01,670 --> 00:54:03,720
We find Sansa Stark a different husband.

847
00:54:03,720 --> 00:54:06,200
- Wonderful. - Yes, it is.

848
00:54:14,580 --> 00:54:15,590
You can't mean it.

849
00:54:16,190 --> 00:54:17,450
I can and I do.

850
00:54:17,470 --> 00:54:19,990
Joffrey has made this poor girl's life miserable

851
00:54:20,000 --> 00:54:22,050
since the day he took her father's head.

852
00:54:22,720 --> 00:54:25,470
Now she's finally free of him and you give her to me?

853
00:54:25,570 --> 00:54:27,110
That's cruel even for you.

854
00:54:27,110 --> 00:54:28,820
Do you intend on mistreating her?

855
00:54:28,880 --> 00:54:30,670
The girl's happiness is not my concern,

856
00:54:30,670 --> 00:54:33,500
- nor should it be yours. - She's a child!

857
00:54:33,560 --> 00:54:34,840
She's flowered, I assure you.

858
00:54:34,840 --> 00:54:36,140
She and I have discussed it at length.

859
00:54:36,140 --> 00:54:38,130
There, you see? You will wed her,

860
00:54:38,130 --> 00:54:40,030
bed her, and put a child in her.

861
00:54:40,200 --> 00:54:42,670
- Surely you're capable of that. - And if I refuse?

862
00:54:42,670 --> 00:54:45,550
You wanted to be rewarded for your valor in battle.

863
00:54:45,820 --> 00:54:49,290
Sansa Stark is a finer reward than you could ever dare hope for.

864
00:54:49,940 --> 00:54:52,370
And it is past time you were wed.

865
00:54:52,370 --> 00:54:53,660
I was wed.

866
00:54:55,210 --> 00:54:56,540
Or don't you remember?

867
00:54:59,350 --> 00:55:00,650
Only too well.

868
00:55:02,080 --> 00:55:04,070
You should be thanking the gods for this.

869
00:55:04,070 --> 00:55:06,210
This is more than you deserve.

870
00:55:06,920 --> 00:55:08,170
Tyrion will do as he's bid.

871
00:55:09,540 --> 00:55:10,470
As will you.

872
00:55:12,700 --> 00:55:13,480
What do you mean?

873
00:55:14,520 --> 00:55:15,890
You'll marry Ser Loras.

874
00:55:18,910 --> 00:55:20,810
- I will not. - The boy is heir to Highgarden.

875
00:55:20,810 --> 00:55:23,280
Tyrion will secure the North, you will secure the Reach.

876
00:55:23,280 --> 00:55:25,710
- No, I won't do it. - Yes, you will.

877
00:55:26,670 --> 00:55:28,880
You're still fertile. You need to marry again and breed.

878
00:55:28,880 --> 00:55:30,760
I am Queen Regent, not some broodmare.

879
00:55:30,760 --> 00:55:32,470
You're my daughter!

880
00:55:34,010 --> 00:55:35,060
You will do as I command

881
00:55:35,060 --> 00:55:37,600
and you will marry Loras Tyrell

882
00:55:38,230 --> 00:55:42,630
and put an end to the disgusting rumors about you once and for all.

883
00:55:43,090 --> 00:55:44,740
Father, don't make me do it again, please.

884
00:55:44,740 --> 00:55:46,230
Not another word.

885
00:55:47,880 --> 00:55:49,070
My children.

886
00:55:51,190 --> 00:55:54,100
You've disgraced the Lannister name for far too long.

887
00:56:06,240 --> 00:56:09,420
*It's always summer*

888
00:56:09,750 --> 00:56:12,660
*Under the sea*

889
00:56:13,060 --> 00:56:15,370
*I know, I know*

890
00:56:15,880 --> 00:56:18,900
*Oh, oh, oh*

891
00:56:19,500 --> 00:56:23,210
*The birds have scales*

892
00:56:23,500 --> 00:56:26,930
*And the fish take wing*

893
00:56:27,330 --> 00:56:29,650
*I know, I know*

894
00:56:30,030 --> 00:56:33,010
*Oh, oh, oh*

895
00:56:33,860 --> 00:56:37,000
*The rain is dry*

896
00:56:37,450 --> 00:56:40,070
*And snow falls up*

897
00:56:40,710 --> 00:56:43,100
*I know, I know*

898
00:56:43,610 --> 00:56:46,530
*Oh, oh, oh*

899
00:56:47,280 --> 00:56:50,790
*The stones crack open*

900
00:56:51,250 --> 00:56:54,400
*The water burns*

901
00:56:55,340 --> 00:56:59,040
*The shadows come to dance*

902
00:56:59,330 --> 00:57:01,210
*My lord*

903
00:57:01,890 --> 00:57:04,660
*The shadows come*

904
00:57:05,090 --> 00:57:07,180
*To play*

905
00:57:07,810 --> 00:57:11,240
*The shadows come to dance*

906
00:57:11,910 --> 00:57:13,580
*My lord*

907
00:57:14,390 --> 00:57:16,830
*The shadows come*

908
00:57:17,470 --> 00:57:20,630
*To stay.*

